INFERENCE 3 finding(s) · 1 serious
========================================================================

  [NEW · SERIOUS · FACT] The expansion was only downward: KEYNOTE-942 already enrolled stage IV, so the upper end did not change; IIB, IIC, and IIIA are all lower-risk stages added below the earlier trial's floor of IIIB.
     quote         : “the Phase 3 enrolled stage IIB–IV, widening it at both ends — down into IIB and IIC, and into IIIA, none of which the earlier trial included”
     evidence says : INTerpath-001 widened the population downward only, adding stage IIB, IIC, and IIIA below KEYNOTE-942's lower boundary of IIIB; the upper boundary (stage IV) was unchanged.
     fix           : the Phase 3 enrolled stage IIB–IV, widening it downward — adding IIB, IIC, and IIIA below the earlier trial's floor of IIIB; the upper boundary, stage IV, was already included

  [NEW · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The sentence is correct for a two-sided 95% CI / alpha=0.05 framework, but it omits that the prespecified one-sided 90% CI (corresponding to the trial's registered one-sided alpha=0.10) would not cross 1.0 — leaving the reader to infer that the CI crossing 1.0 is a neutral, framework-independent fact, when it is only a feature of the two-sided framing the draft is critiquing.
     quote         : “The confidence interval is the tell: 0.309–1.017 crosses 1.0, which is exactly what a two-sided test keys on.”
     evidence says : The 95% CI crossing 1.0 is consistent with the two-sided p=0.053 exceeding 0.05; under the prespecified one-sided framework at alpha=0.10, the corresponding 90% CI would not cross 1.0, which is why the trial's own threshold was met.
     fix           : The confidence interval is the tell: 0.309–1.017 crosses 1.0, which is exactly what a two-sided 95% CI keys on — but the same data, read against the prespecified one-sided 90% CI, would not cross it.

  [NEW · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The one-sided p = 0.0266 also appears in the ASCO 2023 conference abstract (ASCO abstract LBA9503), which is a peer-reviewed publication, not only in the company press release; characterising it as purely a company figure overstates the distinction.
     quote         : “The source of the one-sided p = 0.0266, which is a company figure and not a journal one.”
     evidence says : The one-sided p = 0.0266 appears in both the April 2023 company press release and the ASCO 2023 conference abstract; the Lancet peer-reviewed paper is the source that switched to two-sided p = 0.053.
     fix           : The source of the one-sided p = 0.0266 — a figure that appears in the company release and the ASCO conference abstract, but not in the peer-reviewed Lancet publication, which reported two-sided p = 0.053 instead.

