  What this piece can add that careful coverage does not:
     No outlet found — including the most careful specialist coverage — discussed the OS interval's actual width (0.165–1.345) and what it means arithmetically, the descriptive-only status of the five-year KEYNOTE-942 analyses and why that matters for interpreting the interval clearing 1.0, the one-sided versus two-sided p-value distinction and the trial's own prespecified alpha of 0.10, the investigator-assessed endpoint detail in the Phase 3 and how blinding partially but not fully addresses it, or the absolute RFS percentage rates alongside the hazard ratios. These are the layers the draft uniquely adds beneath even the most careful reporting.

